<https://ekgf.org/ontology/raw#75pct>
    rdfs:label "75th percentile"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Records the 75th-percentile summary value for a captured column."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/raw#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/raw#Column>
    rdfs:label "Column"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A physical field position in exactly one captured raw-data view, linked through isColumnInView or inverse hasColumn. Its identity is independent of its mapped predicate; source metadata and optional statistics describe the column."@en .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/raw#File>
    rdfs:label "File"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A file used as a raw-data source during the capture step of a DataOps pipeline."@en .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/raw#Row>
    rdfs:label "Row"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A record encountered in exactly one raw-data view, retaining its source identifier, sequence position, and captured value occurrences. Each occurrence identifies this row through valueOf and its physical source column through forColumn."@en .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/raw#Source>
    rdfs:label "Source"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "An input data source captured as RDF before transformation into higher-level domain ontologies. A source may expose several views."@en .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/raw#Value>
    rdfs:label "Value"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A captured value occurrence at one source row and one physical column belonging to the same view. It carries one source-supplied RDF literal through literalValue, or is explicitly classified as NullValue. Optional sourceText preserves original textual representation. A mapped predicate is separate from the occurrence's physical location."@en .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/raw#View>
    rdfs:label "View"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A tabular or record-oriented view within a captured source, organizing the rows and columns exposed by that source."@en .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/raw#XlsxFile>
    rdfs:label "XLSX file"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A raw-data file source in the Excel XLSX workbook format."@en .

